  "title": "Composite atoms",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Proved by hand: a knot sphere with flat states at every line, carrying good closed atoms (free, with exactly one unsatisfiable class) at any lines, is again a good closed atom, unsatisfiable exactly where every atom inside acts; so it acts as its line, less any point, exactly where all its atoms act, and composites nest to any depth (theorem N). A composite of genus g holds at least g - 1 units in its region, and g where it acts (lemma U). Computed: the AND at all 274 removed points of seven named composites (as stated off the replaced lines and on them; read on the closed composite inside the leaves).",
